30,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Mizuki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The post-occupancy data is clear. Projects that serve the whole campus are rated far higher than those for one wing.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,My data confirms the pain. We paid for off-site space for two terms because the timetable could not absorb the loss.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,I found that the technicians are doing hours of manual work that the equipment should be doing.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"My schedule data shows a pattern. Projects justified by inspection findings are on time, but comfort projects slip.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The tender data is grim. Mechanical and ducted plant lots are up by about a fifth, while surfacing held near the index.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Mizuki, that explains the disappointment. We keep funding comfort projects that fail to deliver on time.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, and the cost of that delay is not just money, it is the disruption to teaching.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Benjamin, if the plant is so expensive, we must be very careful about what we specify.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, exactly. The weather data shows we lose six weeks to rain on exposed work.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"I also found that the audiovisual kit is written down, but no reserve was opened to replace it.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"So we have a choice. We can fund a project that is cheap to build but serves few, or one that is expensive but serves many.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"The booking data is decisive. General rooms are full, specialist rooms are empty. We must fund the general space.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"I agree. And if we automate the manual routines, we free up the technicians for the work that actually needs them.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"The risk is the schedule. If we choose a project with exposed work, we will lose six weeks to weather.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,The cost risk is real. The plant is up a fifth. We need a plan that avoids the most volatile items.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I am leaning toward the general-use space. It serves the most people and the data supports it.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Victoria,,I am with you. The timetable impact is manageable if we plan the phasing carefully.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,I support it. The automation of the manual routines is a key part of the value.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I am concerned about the delay risk, but the benefit is too large to ignore.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I will support it, provided we lock the plant prices now. The market is not going to wait for us.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
